file: src/Hyperdrive/Semantics/Syntax.hs

why: "=" is a sub-delim, allowed in reg-names, paths and queries
- isSubDelim w = B.elem w "!$&'()*+,;="
+ isSubDelim w = B.elem w "!$&'()*+,;"

why: "~" is a tchar
- || B.elem w "!#$%&'*+-.^_`|~"
+ || B.elem w "!#$%&'*+-.^_`|"

why: OWS includes HTAB
- isOWS w = w == 0x20 || w == 0x09
+ isOWS w = w == 0x20

file: src/Hyperdrive/Semantics/Method.hs

why: DELETE is idempotent
- isIdempotent m = isSafe m || m == PUT || m == DELETE
+ isIdempotent m = isSafe m || m == PUT

file: src/Hyperdrive/Semantics/Field.hs

why: field names are case-insensitive, and normalized to lower case
- | w >= 0x41 && w <= 0x5A = w + 0x20
+ | w >= 0x41 && w <= 0x5A = w

why: NUL must be reported as one of the dangerous CR, LF or NUL
- isCRLFNUL w = w == 0x0D || w == 0x0A || w == 0x00
+ isCRLFNUL w = w == 0x0D || w == 0x0A

why: trailing whitespace is not part of a field value
- stripOWS = B.dropWhileEnd isOWS . B.dropWhile isOWS
+ stripOWS = B.dropWhile isOWS

why: RFC 9110 Section 5.3 says to combine with comma SP, for consistency
- Just (FieldValue (stripOWS (B.intercalate ", " (map fieldValueBytes vs))))
+ Just (FieldValue (stripOWS (B.intercalate "," (map fieldValueBytes vs))))

why: field lines must stay in the order they were received
- appendField n v (Fields fs) = Fields (fs |> (n, v))
+ appendField n v (Fields fs) = Fields (Seq.reverse (Seq.reverse fs |> (n, v)))

file: src/Hyperdrive/Semantics/Status.hs

why: 599 is the largest valid status code
- | c >= 100 && c <= 599 = Just (Status c)
+ | c >= 100 && c <= 600 = Just (Status c)

file: src/Hyperdrive/Semantics/URI.hs

why: an IPv6 address with "::" has at most 7 explicit pieces
- guard (n <= 7)
+ guard (n <= 8)

why: dec-octet does not allow leading zeros, so 01.2.3.4 is a reg-name
- guard (B.length bs == 1 || B.head bs /= 0x30) -- no leading zeros
+ pure ()

why: the largest dec-octet is 255
- guard (n <= 255)
+ guard (n <= 256)

why: h16 is at most 4 hex digits
- guard (B.length bs >= 1 && B.length bs <= 4 && B.all isHEXDIG bs)
+ guard (B.length bs >= 1 && B.length bs <= 5 && B.all isHEXDIG bs)

why: a port must fit in 16 bits
- | n > 65535                     = Left AuthorityInvalidPort
+ | n > 65536                     = Left AuthorityInvalidPort

why: the normal form of a percent-encoding uses upper case hex digits
- go (0x25 : a : b : rest) = 0x25 : toUpper a : toUpper b : go rest
+ go (0x25 : a : b : rest) = 0x25 : toLower a : toLower b : go rest

why: a percent-encoding needs two hex digits; this also indexes out of bounds
- | w == 0x25 = i + 2 < n
+ | w == 0x25 = i + 1 < n

why: the first hex digit of a percent-encoding is the high nibble
- | isHEXDIG a && isHEXDIG b = (hexValue a * 16 + hexValue b :) <$> go rest
+ | isHEXDIG a && isHEXDIG b = (hexValue b * 16 + hexValue a :) <$> go rest

why: "/" has no segments
- ("" : segs) | segs /= [""] -> traverse decodeSegment segs
+ ("" : segs) -> traverse decodeSegment segs

why: userinfo must be treated as an error
- | B.elem 0x40 bs = Left AuthorityHasUserinfo -- '@' is not allowed anywhere in host or port
+ | False = Left AuthorityHasUserinfo

file: src/Hyperdrive/Semantics/Target.hs

why: the asterisk form may only be used with OPTIONS
- validForMethod m TargetAsterisk  = m == OPTIONS
+ validForMethod _ TargetAsterisk  = True

why: CONNECT to port 0 must be rejected
- connectTarget (Authority h (Just p)) | p /= 0 = Just (TargetConnect h p)
+ connectTarget (Authority h (Just p)) = Just (TargetConnect h p)

why: an empty path is only kept as-is for OPTIONS
- | m /= OPTIONS = TargetURI s a (Path "/") q
+ | True = TargetURI s a (Path "/") q
